<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared hook copy check, as a consumer keeps it in
.github/workflows/hook-copy.yml. The rendered file is the whole of the
consumer's hook copy check job: the steps live in
.github/workflows/hook-copy.yml of the shared repository, named here by
commit with the version as a comment; before the first release the comment
carries no version (decision record 0024, decision record 0056).

Required check: "Hook copy". The forge reports the calling job only as
"Hook copy / Hook copy". The job `result` reports "Hook copy" and fails
unless the call passed; the engine reads it as covering the calling job
(cordanaLLM/praetor#1212, decision record 0030).

Fields: .Shared.Repository, .Shared.Commit and .Shared.Version are working
names until the engine renders caller templates (cordanaLLM/praetor#1211);
.RunnerTag is the engine's own. The trigger is spelled out for the same reason:
with the engine it becomes the hosted gate's trigger function.

Concurrency is set here and not in the shared workflow, so a consumer's group
never collides with another caller's.

Licence header: the rendered caller starts with the consumer's own header,
written from .Licence (working names, as above), so the consumer's licence
check accepts it (#3). The REUSE-IgnoreStart and REUSE-IgnoreEnd notes render
as nothing and keep this repository's licence check from reading the field
lines as tags.
*/ -%>
<%- /* REUSE-IgnoreStart */ -%>
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: <% .Licence.CopyrightText %>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: <% .Licence.Identifier %>
<%/* REUSE-IgnoreEnd */ -%>
---
# Hook copy: verify the caller's hook copies match the shared repository.
# The job is the shared workflow of <% .Shared.Repository %>, named by commit.
name: Hook copy

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]
  push:
    branches: [main]
  merge_group:

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: hook-copy-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

jobs:
  hook-copy:
    name: Hook copy
    permissions:
      contents: read
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/hook-copy.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      runner: <% .RunnerTag %>

  # The forge reports the calling job above only as "Hook copy / Hook copy",
  # never as "Hook copy". This job reports "Hook copy" and fails unless the
  # hook copy check passed; it runs under always() so a failed or cancelled
  # check still reports here.
  result:
    name: Hook copy
    needs: hook-copy
    if: always()
    runs-on: <% .RunnerTag %>
    timeout-minutes: 5
    permissions: {}
    steps:
      - name: Fail unless the hook copy check passed
        if: needs.hook-copy.result != 'success'
        shell: bash
        run: |
          echo "The hook copy check did not pass."
          exit 1
